  "final_text": "I created the dashboard and the alert rule, and the rule is enabled. It has run once and reported status `ok`, which means the query ran without errors. I couldn't confirm the 5xx query matches any documents, because Kibana's console proxy is turned off in this setup.\n\n**1. Fields in the data.** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` view (time field `timestamp`) contains web access logs:\n- **Request details:** `request`, `url`, `extension`, `referer` and `agent`.\n- **Response:** `response`, the HTTP status code. It's stored as a string, with an exact-match `response.keyword` version.\n- **Payload:** `bytes`.\n- **Client:** `clientip`, `machine.os` and `machine.ram`.\n- **Location:** `geo.src` (source country), `geo.dest` and `geo.coordinates`.\n- **Other:** `host`, `tags` and `memory`.\n\n**2. Dashboard: `EFF-fb63fdc6 Web logs overview`** (id `eff-fb63fdc6-web-logs-overview-9fde49fc4e42`) has seven panels:\n- Total requests (number)\n- Unique visitors (distinct `clientip`)\n- Total bytes served (sum of `bytes`)\n- Requests over time, split by response code (bar chart)\n- Response code breakdown (pie chart)\n- Top requested URLs, with request count and average bytes (table)\n- Traffic by source country (bar chart)\n\n**3. Alert rule: `EFF-fb63fdc6 5xx spike`** (id `94c35eb8-6792-43b1-9a1a-648c098e77e2`)\n- It runs every minute and counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` from the last 5 minutes, using the `timestamp` field.\n- A response is treated as 5xx when `response.keyword` starts with \"5\". The rule fires when the count is more than 10.\n- It has no actions attached, so a firing alert shows up in Kibana but sends no notifications. If you want notifications, a connector such as Slack or email would need to be added.",
